meta {
  name: Resend verification email
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

post {
  url: {{host}}/api/auth/resend-verification
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

docs {
  UC-15. Authenticated.

  No body: the person is read from the bearer token, so a caller can only ever ask for their own link. An address that is already verified answers 400.

  A link mailed to the person within HEIMDALL_ADMIN_EMAIL_COOLDOWN_IN_SECONDS (five minutes by default) — the one sent at account creation, an administrator's, or an earlier resend — answers 429 "An email of this kind was sent to you recently. Try again in a few minutes." and sends nothing. The endpoint is also rate-limited per client address: its 429 says "Too many requests." and carries Retry-After.
}
